@@ -4,6 +4,15 @@ Shunter uses source versions from `VERSION` and release tags named `vX.Y.Z`.
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Added `ReducerDB.TableID(name string) (uint32, bool)` to resolve recovered
+  table IDs during a reducer invocation; unknown names and expired handles
+  return false. Custom implementations and test doubles must add the method.
+- Durable batches preserve sparse offset-index byte cadence while continuing
+  to sync the backing index after the log. Rotation and close retain the final
+  candidate; durability and delivery guarantees are unchanged. Sparse hints can
+  increase recovery scanning, and inherited full indexes are not resampled.
+- Buffered snapshot file writes independently of hashing. Flush failures stop
+  before hash-header patching, syncing or atomic publication.
 - Added a reproducible external canary capacity study covering hosted latency,
   fanout, server memory during writes and snapshots, and offline backup/restore
   up to a 37.317 MiB fixture. Recorded measurements remain advisory.
